MINOR-2 — SIG-5 self-match protection incomplete against concurrent instances/carriers
======================================================================

Live-concurrency reproduction NOTE (§11.4.6 honest boundary): an attempt
to spawn a real long-lived decoy 'grep -qE <pattern-shaped-arg>' process
and locate it via 'pgrep -x grep' was confounded by this specific
sandboxed tool-execution environment, which wraps every Bash tool call
in its own '/bin/bash -c ...' harness and leaves multiple unrelated
pre-existing comm=grep processes on the host (e.g. a libtinfo-warning
filter) — pgrep -x grep repeatedly resolved to the WRONG pid, an
instance of the exact §11.4.201(7)(a) carrier-ambiguity class this
MINOR is about. Chasing a clean live reproduction inside this sandbox
further was not a productive use of remaining budget; the fix is
instead validated two ways below: (1) a deterministic logic-level test
of the EXACT shipped comm-exclusion code (extracted verbatim from the
file, never retyped), and (2) the full §11.4.115(F) polarity re-run
(minor-4.log) proving SIG-5 detection is UNCHANGED for both the real-
incident class (comm=ugrep) and the fixture's disguised-argv class
(comm=bash) after this fix landed — i.e. no regression.

--- (1) Deterministic logic-level test of the exact shipped exclusion ---
Extracting the real case-statement from the shipped script (single
source of truth, never hand-retyped):
  case "$COMM" in
    grep|awk|ps) continue ;;
  esac

Test harness (sources the extracted snippet against synthetic COMM values):
  comm=grep       -> EXCLUDED (skipped from SIG-5 candidacy)
  comm=awk        -> EXCLUDED (skipped from SIG-5 candidacy)
  comm=ps         -> EXCLUDED (skipped from SIG-5 candidacy)
  comm=bash       -> NOT excluded (still a SIG-5 candidate)
  comm=ugrep      -> NOT excluded (still a SIG-5 candidate)
  comm=sh         -> NOT excluded (still a SIG-5 candidate)
  comm=python3    -> NOT excluded (still a SIG-5 candidate)

Expected + verified: grep/awk/ps EXCLUDED (closes the concurrent-instance
/ source-grep self-match vector — MINOR-2); bash NOT excluded (preserves
the RED fixture's disguised-argv detection class); ugrep NOT excluded
(preserves the real-incident detection class).

--- (2) §1.1 paired mutation: strip the exclusion, confirm it is load-bearing ---
Mutated case statement (exclusion effectively disabled):
  case "$COMM" in
    never-matches-anything) continue ;;
  esac
  MUTATED: comm=grep   -> excluded=0 (expect 0 — mutation removes the guard)
  MUTATED: comm=awk    -> excluded=0 (expect 0 — mutation removes the guard)
  MUTATED: comm=ps     -> excluded=0 (expect 0 — mutation removes the guard)

======================================================================
--- (3) Regression proof: full polarity re-run, SIG-5 real-incident +
        fixture-disguise detection classes both still fire ---
See minor-4.log for the full 5/5 RED CONFIRMED transcript from this
same remediation round (includes: 'SIG-5  RED CONFIRMED').

VERDICT: FIXED. Logic-level test (1) proves the shipped exclusion
classifies exactly the intended process classes; the mutation test (2)
proves the guard is load-bearing (mutated version excludes nothing);
the polarity re-run (3) proves zero regression in real detection power.
